      "writtenOn": "2023-10-16T09:19:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it\u0027s better to keep this short method here for reasons:\n1. it\u0027s for argument checking of only `registerService` and `discoverServices` API, I don\u0027t see  generic use cases. Or you can share if there are?\n2. It\u0027s easier to read the definition of the short method by keeping the method close to where it\u0027s used - so that you don\u0027t need to jump into different files; It\u0027s also a practice I am following that I usually group private an public methods together if they are logically relevant (It\u0027s the case for this method).\n\nI would prefer keeping it as is if you don\u0027t have a strong preference.\n\n\u003e it will could make the test those function easier\n\nCan you elaborate on this? If we want to write unit tests for this private method, we can use \"@VisibleForTesting\", I don\u0027t see why it\u0027s easier to move this method to MdnsUtils.java.",
      "parentUuid": "8fee9e84_0bb96d93",
      "revId": "b54f7d31d8fbc5a8c457b79d4a56049b72a1d36a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
